{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01V3idHxT476cgp8Ub34NBUB","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t# Report: Batch Stacked Reduction MLE Sync\n2\t\n3\t## Description\n4\t\n5\tThe stacked reduction MLE rounds in `batch_sumcheck_poly_eval()` performed a synchronous D2H copy (`to_host()` with full GPU pipeline drain) per trace-matrix window per MLE round. With ~400+ windows and 17 MLE rounds at APC 300, this created ~7,000+ pipeline-draining sync points per segment. Both CUDA kernels already use atomic accumulation into a shared `d_accum` buffer, and the final result is a sum across all windows, so per-window syncs are unnecessary. This optimization replaces them with a single `fill_zero` + `to_host` per round (~17 syncs per segment total), eliminating the dominant source of CPU-GPU synchronization overhead."}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"bf8cf1a6-3d58-4ca0-8a0c-442b3fb4c97c","uuid":"95ef369d-12ef-4246-b0e3-2929feabe9b7","timestamp":"2026-04-12T22:10:28.589Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/home/georg/stark-backend/autoopt-results/2026-04-12-2330-batch-stacked-reduction-mle-sync/report.md","content":"# Report: Batch Stacked Reduction MLE Sync\n\n## Description\n\nThe stacked reduction MLE rounds in `batch_sumcheck_poly_eval()` performed a synchronous D2H copy (`to_host()` with full GPU pipeline drain) per trace-matrix window per MLE round. With ~400+ windows and 17 MLE rounds at APC 300, this created ~7,000+ pipeline-draining sync points per segment. Both CUDA kernels already use atomic accumulation into a shared `d_accum` buffer, and the final result is a sum across all windows, so per-window syncs are unnecessary. This optimization replaces them with a single `fill_zero` + `to_host` per round (~17 syncs per segment total), eliminating the dominant source of CPU-GPU synchronization overhead.","numLines":5,"startLine":1,"totalLines":88}}}
