{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-6","id":"msg_01YFUSBn5KXCsnKmzrmXXeUN","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_017uHSfmrKxvHbyR6VsvKSjT","name":"Write","input":{"file_path":"/home/georg/stark-backend/autoopt-results/task.md","content":"# 2026-04-13-0100-multistream-round0-parallel\n\nRound 0 constraint evaluation processes 623 AIRs sequentially on a single CUDA stream (cudaStreamPerThread). At APC 300, most AIRs are tiny (height 8-64), so each kernel uses 1-4 of the RTX 4090's 128 SMs — GPU throughput drops 10.7x per cell vs APC 0. By processing AIRs across N OS threads (each with its own per-thread CUDA stream), small kernels from different streams execute concurrently on idle SMs, recovering GPU utilization and overlapping CPU metadata preparation with GPU execution. This is expected to reduce Round 0 from ~663ms to ~350-430ms (35-48% improvement), yielding an 8-14% reduction in STARK excl trace.\n"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1023,"cache_read_input_tokens":135445,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1023},"output_tokens":53,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"bf8cf1a6-3d58-4ca0-8a0c-442b3fb4c97c","uuid":"232019aa-5ae8-4a28-9bce-858a824ca78a"}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_017uHSfmrKxvHbyR6VsvKSjT","type":"tool_result","content":"The file /home/georg/stark-backend/autoopt-results/task.md has been updated successfully."}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"bf8cf1a6-3d58-4ca0-8a0c-442b3fb4c97c","uuid":"d2e20c60-16f1-47f8-9a02-32bb0eea5e22","timestamp":"2026-04-12T22:35:31.165Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"update","filePath":"/home/georg/stark-backend/autoopt-results/task.md","content":"# 2026-04-13-0100-multistream-round0-parallel\n\nRound 0 constraint evaluation processes 623 AIRs sequentially on a single CUDA stream (cudaStreamPerThread). At APC 300, most AIRs are tiny (height 8-64), so each kernel uses 1-4 of the RTX 4090's 128 SMs — GPU throughput drops 10.7x per cell vs APC 0. By processing AIRs across N OS threads (each with its own per-thread CUDA stream), small kernels from different streams execute concurrently on idle SMs, recovering GPU utilization and overlapping CPU metadata preparation with GPU execution. This is expected to reduce Round 0 from ~663ms to ~350-430ms (35-48% improvement), yielding an 8-14% reduction in STARK excl trace.\n","structuredPatch":[{"oldStart":1,"oldLines":3,"newStart":1,"newLines":3,"lines":["-# 2026-04-12-2330-batch-stacked-reduction-mle-sync","+# 2026-04-13-0100-multistream-round0-parallel"," ","-The stacked reduction MLE rounds in `batch_sumcheck_poly_eval()` perform a synchronous D2H copy (`to_host()` with full GPU pipeline drain) per height group per round. With ~400+ height groups and 17 MLE rounds, this creates ~7,000+ pipeline-draining sync points per segment. Since both the regular and degenerate CUDA kernels already use atomic accumulation into a shared `d_accum` buffer, and the final result is a sum across all windows, these per-window syncs are unnecessary — a single `fill_zero` + `to_host` per round suffices. This eliminates the dominant source of CPU-GPU synchronization overhead, which profiling shows accounts for the majority of the 287ms MLE rounds time at APC 300 (vs ~60ms of actual GPU kernel time).","+Round 0 constraint evaluation processes 623 AIRs sequentially on a single CUDA stream (cudaStreamPerThread). At APC 300, most AIRs are tiny (height 8-64), so each kernel uses 1-4 of the RTX 4090's 128 SMs — GPU throughput drops 10.7x per cell vs APC 0. By processing AIRs across N OS threads (each with its own per-thread CUDA stream), small kernels from different streams execute concurrently on idle SMs, recovering GPU utilization and overlapping CPU metadata preparation with GPU execution. This is expected to reduce Round 0 from ~663ms to ~350-430ms (35-48% improvement), yielding an 8-14% reduction in STARK excl trace."]}],"originalFile":"# 2026-04-12-2330-batch-stacked-reduction-mle-sync\n\nThe stacked reduction MLE rounds in `batch_sumcheck_poly_eval()` perform a synchronous D2H copy (`to_host()` with full GPU pipeline drain) per height group per round. With ~400+ height groups and 17 MLE rounds, this creates ~7,000+ pipeline-draining sync points per segment. Since both the regular and degenerate CUDA kernels already use atomic accumulation into a shared `d_accum` buffer, and the final result is a sum across all windows, these per-window syncs are unnecessary — a single `fill_zero` + `to_host` per round suffices. This eliminates the dominant source of CPU-GPU synchronization overhead, which profiling shows accounts for the majority of the 287ms MLE rounds time at APC 300 (vs ~60ms of actual GPU kernel time).\n"}}
