tx.cached_mains,\n        common_main: &air_ctx.common_main,\n        eq_xis: &self.eq_xis,\n        d_lambda_pows,\n        beta_pows: &self.beta_pows,\n        l_skip,\n        constraint_degree: self.constraint_degree,\n        xi,\n        max_temp_bytes: self.memory_limit_bytes,\n    }\n}).collect();\n\n// Ensure all prior GPU work is visible to worker thread streams.\n// This is required because cudaStreamPerThread in worker threads\n// are distinct streams that do not automatically synchronize with\n// the main thread's stream.\ncurrent_stream_sync()?;\n\n// Phase 2: Process AIRs in parallel across N OS threads\nlet num_threads = std::cmp::min(work_items.len(), NUM_ROUND0_STREAMS);\nlet results: Vec<Round0AirResult> = if num_threads <= 1 {\n    // Fallback: sequential processing (same as before)\n    work_items.iter()\n        .map(|w| process_air_round0(w))\n        .collect::<Result<Vec<_>, _>>()?\n} else {\n    let chunk_size = (work_items.len() + num_threads - 1) / num_threads;\n    std::thread::scope(|s| {\n        let handles: Vec<_> = work_items\n            .chunks(chunk_size)\n            .map(|chunk| {\n                s.spawn(move || {\n                    chunk.iter()\n                        .map(|w| process_air_round0(w))\n                        .collect::<Result<Vec<_>, _>>()\n                })\n            })\n            .collect();\n        let mut all_results = Vec::with_capacity(work_items.len());\n        for handle in handles {\n            all_results.extend(handle.join().unwrap()?);\n        }\n        Ok::<_, LogupZerocheckError>(all_results)\n    })?\n};\n\n// Phase 3: Scatter results into batch_sp_poly (main thread)\nfor result in results {\n    if let Some(poly) = result.zerocheck_poly {\n        batch_sp_poly[2 * num_present_airs + result.trace_idx] = poly;\n    }\n    if let Some(poly) = result.logup_numer_poly {\n        batch_sp_poly[2 * result.trace_idx] = poly;\n    }\n    if let Some(poly) = result.logup_denom_poly {\n        batch_sp_poly[2 * result.trace_idx + 1] = poly;\n    }\n}\n```\n\n**Why:** Phase 1 is pure CPU (no GPU interaction). Phase 2 spawns N OS threads; each thread gets its own CUDA stream via `cudaStreamPerThread`. The GPU can execute small kernels from different streams concurrently on idle SMs. Phase 3 is a trivial scatter.\n\n### Change 4: Add configurable thread count constant\n\n**File:** `crates/cuda-backend/src/logup_zerocheck/mod.rs`\n\n**What:** Add a constant near the top of the file:\n\n```rust\n/// Number of OS threads (and thus CUDA streams) for parallel Round 0 processing.\n/// Each thread gets its own per-thread CUDA stream. More threads = more concurrent\n/// kernels, but also more peak GPU memory for intermediate buffers.\nconst NUM_ROUND0_STREAMS: usize = 4;\n```\n\n**Why:** Controls the parallelism level. 4 is a good starting point: enough to fill the GPU with small kernels without excessive memory overhead. Can be tuned based on profiling.\n\n## Invariants\n\n1. **Correctness**: Each AIR's constraint and interaction evaluations are independent. The output polynomials in `batch_sp_poly` are written to disjoint indices (`trace_idx`). The final result is identical regardless of processing order.\n\n2. **Memory ordering**: `current_stream_sync()` before spawning threads ensures all prior GPU work (trace matrices, proving key data, selector uploads) is visible to worker thread streams. Within each worker thread, operations are ordered by its per-thread stream.\n\n3. **DeviceBuffer lifetimes**: Intermediate buffers (`temp_sums_buffer`, `intermediates`) are allocated on the worker thread's stream via `cudaMallocAsync(cudaStreamPerThread)` and freed when dropped (still on the same thread). No cross-stream memory ownership.\n\n4. **D2H copies**: `to_host_on_current_stream()` syncs only the calling thread's stream. Each thread's D2H is independent. The global `COPY_EVENT` is not used in the parallel path.\n\n5. **Fallback path**: When `num_threads <= 1` (or