{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01XeZXPKZ9d8JHARDhMDNPh8","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t# Plan: Multi-stream Round 0 Parallel AIR Processing\n2\t\n3\t## Goal\n4\t\n5\tReduce Round 0 wall-clock time at APC 300 by processing AIRs across multiple OS threads, each with its own CUDA stream (`cudaStreamPerThread`). Small kernels from different streams execute concurrently on idle SMs of the RTX 4090, improving GPU utilization from <5% (height-8 AIRs on 1/128 SMs) to 20-50% (4-8 concurrent kernels on different SMs).\n6\t\n7\tTarget: Round 0 from 663ms to ~350-430ms (35-48% improvement). STARK excl trace from 2272ms to ~1950-2100ms (8-14% improvement).\n8\t\n9\t## Current Code Path\n10\t\n11\t### Entry point\n12\t`crates/cuda-backend/src/logup_zerocheck/mod.rs:598` — `sumcheck_uni_round0_polys()`\n13\t\n14\t### Setup phase (lines 598-728, unchanged)\n15\tPre-computes shared data: `eq_xis` hash map, lambda powers, logup combinations, eq_3b weights, selector bases. All this data is read-only during the per-AIR loop. Runs on the main thread.\n16\t\n17\t### Per-AIR loop (lines 732-880, the target)\n18\tIterates over `ctx.per_trace` (623 entries at APC 300). For each AIR:\n19\t\n20\t1. **CPU metadata** (lines 741-772): Extract `SymbolicConstraints`, compute `omega_root`, collect `main_parts` raw pointers, H2D upload `d_main_parts`.\n21\t2. **Constraint kernel** (lines 777-790): `evaluate_round0_constraints_gpu()` in `round0.rs:31-124`. Allocates intermediate + temp_sums DeviceBuffers, launches `zerocheck_ntt_eval_constraints` kernel. Returns `DeviceBuffer<EF>` of size `num_cosets_zc * skip_domain`.\n22\t3. **Constraint D2H + postprocess** (lines 791-827): `sum_buffer.to_host()` (pipeline drain via `COPY_EVENT` mutex), transpose to row-major, iDFT via `UnivariatePoly::from_geometric_cosets_evals_idft`, multiply by `(Z^{2^l_skip} - 1)`.\n23\t4. **Interaction kernel** (lines 831-846): `evaluate_round0_interactions_gpu()` in `round0.rs:132-275`. Builds interaction rules from `SymbolicConstraints`, allocates buffers, launches `logup_bary_eval_interactions_round0` kernel. Returns `DeviceBuffer<Frac<EF>>`.\n24\t5. **Interaction D2H + postprocess** (lines 847-879): `sum.to_host()`, extract numer/denom, transpose, iDFT. Writes to `batch_sp_poly[2*trace_idx]` and `[2*trace_idx+1]`.\n25\t\n26\t### Why it's slow\n27\t- 623 AIRs on one stream: kernels execute sequentially. Small kernels (height 8-64) use 1-4 of 128 SMs.\n28\t- Nsight kernel distribution for Round 0 at APC 300:\n29\t  - <100us: 420 kernels, 20ms total\n30\t  - 100-500us: 783 kernels, 202ms total\n31\t  - 500us-1ms: 322 kernels, 221ms total\n32\t  - >1ms: 55 kernels, 101ms total\n33\t- Total GPU kernel time: 543ms, wall clock: 663ms. Overhead (CPU prep + D2H): 120ms.\n34\t- GPU throughput drops 10.7x per cell from APC 0 to APC 300 due to underutilized SMs.\n35\t\n36\t### Key property enabling parallelism\n37\tEach AIR's processing is **fully independent**: no data flows between AIRs in Round 0. All shared data (`pk`, `eq_xis`, `selectors_base`, trace matrices, `beta_pows`, `d_lambda_pows`) is read-only. `DeviceBuffer<T>` is `Send + Sync` (`crates/cuda-common/src/d_buffer.rs:36-37`). Output slots `batch_sp_poly[trace_idx]` are disjoint per AIR.\n38\t\n39\t## Changes\n40\t\n41\t### Change 1: Add `to_host_on_current_stream()` to DeviceBuffer\n42\t\n43\t**File:** `crates/cuda-common/src/copy.rs`\n44\t\n45\t**What:** Add a new method `to_host_on_current_stream()` to `MemCopyD2H` impl for `DeviceBuffer<T>`. This method uses `cudaStreamSynchronize(cudaStreamPerThread)` instead of `COPY_EVENT.lock().record_and_wait()`, eliminating global mutex contention when called from multiple threads simultaneously.\n46\t\n47\t```rust\n48\tpub trait MemCopyD2HStreamSync<T> {\n49\t    fn to_host_on_current_stream(&self) -> Result<Vec<T>, MemCopyError>;\n50\t}\n51\t\n52\timpl<T> MemCopyD2HStreamSync<T> for DeviceBuffer<T> {\n53\t    fn to_host_on_current_stream(&self) -> Result<Vec<T>, MemCopyError> {\n54\t        let mut host_vec = Vec::with_capacity(self.len());\n55\t        let size_bytes = std::mem::size_of::<T>() * self.len();\n56\t        check(unsafe {\n57\t            cudaMemcpyAsync(\n58\t                host_vec.as_mut_ptr() as *mut c_void,\n59\t                self.as_raw_ptr(),\n60\t                size_bytes,\n61\t                cudaMemcpyKind::cudaMemcpyDeviceToHost,\n62\t                cudaStreamPerThread,\n63\t            )\n64\t        })?;\n65\t        current_stream_sync().map_err(|e| MemCopyError::CopyD2H(e.into()))?;\n66\t        unsafe { host_vec.set_len(self.len()); }\n67\t        Ok(host_vec)\n68\t    }\n69\t}\n70\t```\n71\t\n72\t**Why:** The existing `to_host()` uses a global `Mutex<CudaEvent>` (`COPY_EVENT`). With multi-threaded Round 0, the mutex serializes D2H calls across all threads — while one thread blocks waiting for its kernel (holding the mutex), other threads cannot perform their D2H. `to_host_on_current_stream()` uses per-thread stream synchronization instead, so each thread blocks only on its own stream.\n73\t\n74\t**Note:** For pageable host memory, `cudaMemcpyAsync` is effectively synchronous, so the subsequent `cudaStreamSynchronize` is belt-and-suspenders. Either approach is correct; the key change is eliminating the global mutex.\n75\t\n76\t### Change 2: Extract per-AIR work into a standalone function\n77\t\n78\t**File:** `crates/cuda-backend/src/logup_zerocheck/mod.rs`\n79\t\n80\t**What:** Extract the loop body (lines 741-879) into a new function:\n81\t\n82\t```rust\n83\t/// Result of processing one AIR in Round 0.\n84\tstruct Round0AirResult {\n85\t    trace_idx: usize,\n86\t    zerocheck_poly: Option<UnivariatePoly<EF>>,\n87\t    logup_numer_poly: Option<UnivariatePoly<EF>>,\n88\t    logup_denom_poly: Option<UnivariatePoly<EF>>,\n89\t}\n90\t\n91\t/// All data needed to process one AIR in Round 0 (all references are read-only).\n92\tstruct Round0AirWorkItem<'a, HS: GpuHashScheme> {\n93\t    trace_idx: usize,\n94\t    air_idx: usize,\n95\t    single_pk: &'a DeviceStarkProvingKey<GenericGpuBackend<HS>>,\n96\t    n: i32,\n97\t    selectors_cube: &'a DeviceMatrix<F>,\n98\t    public_values: &'a DeviceBuffer<F>,\n99\t    eq_3bs: &'a [EF],\n100\t    cached_mains: &'a [CommittedTraceData<GenericGpuBackend<HS>>],\n101\t    common_main: &'a DeviceMatrix<F>,\n102\t    eq_xis: &'a FxHashMap<usize, EqEvalLayers<EF>>,\n103\t    d_lambda_pows: &'a DeviceBuffer<EF>,\n104\t    beta_pows: &'a DeviceBuffer<EF>,\n105\t    l_skip: usize,\n106\t    constraint_degree: usize,\n107\t    xi: &'a [EF],\n108\t    max_temp_bytes: usize,\n109\t}\n110\t\n111\tfn process_air_round0<HS: GpuHashScheme>(\n112\t    work: &Round0AirWorkItem<'_, HS>,\n113\t) -> Result<Round0AirResult, LogupZerocheckError> {\n114\t    // Contains the exact logic currently in lines 741-879 of mod.rs,\n115\t    // using to_host_on_current_stream() instead of to_host().\n116\t    // Returns Round0AirResult instead of writing to batch_sp_poly directly.\n117\t    ...\n118\t}\n119\t```\n120\t\n121\t**Why:** The standalone function is callable from any thread. It takes only immutable references to shared data plus the per-AIR identifiers. Each thread invokes this function for its assigned AIRs.\n122\t\n123\t### Change 3: Restructure Round 0 into 3 phases with parallel execution\n124\t\n125\t**File:** `crates/cuda-backend/src/logup_zerocheck/mod.rs`\n126\t\n127\t**What:** Replace the sequential loop (lines 732-880) with a 3-phase structure:\n128\t\n129\t```rust\n130\t// Phase 1: Build work items (main thread, pure CPU)\n131\tlet work_items: Vec<Round0AirWorkItem<HS>> = izip!(\n132\t    &ctx.per_trace, &self.n_per_trace, &selectors_base,\n133\t    &self.public_values_per_trace, &self.eq_3b_per_trace,\n134\t).enumerate().map(|(trace_idx, ((air_idx, air_ctx), &n, sel, pv, eq3b))| {\n135\t    Round0AirWorkItem {\n136\t        trace_idx,\n137\t        air_idx: *air_idx,\n138\t        single_pk: &self.pk.per_air[*air_idx],\n139\t        n,\n140\t        selectors_cube: sel,\n141\t        public_values: pv,\n142\t        eq_3bs: eq3b,\n143\t        cached_mains: &air_ctx.cached_mains,\n144\t        common_main: &air_ctx.common_main,\n145\t        eq_xis: &self.eq_xis,\n146\t        d_lambda_pows,\n147\t        beta_pows: &self.beta_pows,\n148\t        l_skip,\n149\t        constraint_degree: self.constraint_degree,\n150\t        xi,\n151\t        max_temp_bytes: self.memory_limit_bytes,\n152\t    }\n153\t}).collect();\n154\t\n155\t// Ensure all prior GPU work is visible to worker thread streams.\n156\t// This is required because cudaStreamPerThread in worker threads\n157\t// are distinct streams that do not automatically synchronize with\n158\t// the main thread's stream.\n159\tcurrent_stream_sync()?;\n160\t\n161\t// Phase 2: Process AIRs in parallel across N OS threads\n162\tlet num_threads = std::cmp::min(work_items.len(), NUM_ROUND0_STREAMS);\n163\tlet results: Vec<Round0AirResult> = if num_threads <= 1 {\n164\t    // Fallback: sequential processing (same as before)\n165\t    work_items.iter()\n166\t        .map(|w| process_air_round0(w))\n167\t        .collect::<Result<Vec<_>, _>>()?\n168\t} else {\n169\t    let chunk_size = (work_items.len() + num_threads - 1) / num_threads;\n170\t    std::thread::scope(|s| {\n171\t        let handles: Vec<_> = work_items\n172\t            .chunks(chunk_size)\n173\t            .map(|chunk| {\n174\t                s.spawn(move || {\n175\t                    chunk.iter()\n176\t                        .map(|w| process_air_round0(w))\n177\t                        .collect::<Result<Vec<_>, _>>()\n178\t                })\n179\t            })\n180\t            .collect();\n181\t        let mut all_results = Vec::with_capacity(work_items.len());\n182\t        for handle in handles {\n183\t            all_results.extend(handle.join().unwrap()?);\n184\t        }\n185\t        Ok::<_, LogupZerocheckError>(all_results)\n186\t    })?\n187\t};\n188\t\n189\t// Phase 3: Scatter results into batch_sp_poly (main thread)\n190\tfor result in results {\n191\t    if let Some(poly) = result.zerocheck_poly {\n192\t        batch_sp_poly[2 * num_present_airs + result.trace_idx] = poly;\n193\t    }\n194\t    if let Some(poly) = result.logup_numer_poly {\n195\t        batch_sp_poly[2 * result.trace_idx] = poly;\n196\t    }\n197\t    if let Some(poly) = result.logup_denom_poly {\n198\t        batch_sp_poly[2 * result.trace_idx + 1] = poly;\n199\t    }\n200\t}\n201\t```\n202\t\n203\t**Why:** Phase 1 is pure CPU (no GPU interaction). Phase 2 spawns N OS threads; each thread gets its own CUDA stream via `cudaStreamPerThread`. The GPU can execute small kernels from different streams concurrently on idle SMs. Phase 3 is a trivial scatter.\n204\t\n205\t### Change 4: Add configurable thread count constant\n206\t\n207\t**File:** `crates/cuda-backend/src/logup_zerocheck/mod.rs`\n208\t\n209\t**What:** Add a constant near the top of the file:\n210\t\n211\t```rust\n212\t/// Number of OS threads (and thus CUDA streams) for parallel Round 0 processing.\n213\t/// Each thread gets its own per-thread CUDA stream. More threads = more concurrent\n214\t/// kernels, but also more peak GPU memory for intermediate buffers.\n215\tconst NUM_ROUND0_STREAMS: usize = 4;\n216\t```\n217\t\n218\t**Why:** Controls the parallelism level. 4 is a good starting point: enough to fill the GPU with small kernels without excessive memory overhead. Can be tuned based on profiling.\n219\t\n220\t## Invariants\n221\t\n222\t1. **Correctness**: Each AIR's constraint and interaction evaluations are independent. The output polynomials in `batch_sp_poly` are written to disjoint indices (`trace_idx`). The final result is identical regardless of processing order.\n223\t\n224\t2. **Memory ordering**: `current_stream_sync()` before spawning threads ensures all prior GPU work (trace matrices, proving key data, selector uploads) is visible to worker thread streams. Within each worker thread, operations are ordered by its per-thread stream.\n225\t\n226\t3. **DeviceBuffer lifetimes**: Intermediate buffers (`temp_sums_buffer`, `intermediates`) are allocated on the worker thread's stream via `cudaMallocAsync(cudaStreamPerThread)` and freed when dropped (still on the same thread). No cross-stream memory ownership.\n227\t\n228\t4. **D2H copies**: `to_host_on_current_stream()` syncs only the calling thread's stream. Each thread's D2H is independent. The global `COPY_EVENT` is not used in the parallel path.\n229\t\n230\t5. **Fallback path**: When `num_threads <= 1` (or very few AIRs), the code falls back to sequential processing using the same `process_air_round0` function. This ensures no regression for APC 0 workloads or single-AIR cases.\n231\t\n232\t6. **No protocol change**: Only the execution order within the prover changes. The mathematical operations per AIR remain identical. Verifier is unaffected.\n233\t\n234\t## Measurement Plan\n235\t\n236\t### Commands\n237\tRun the benchmark suite in the powdr repo:\n238\t```bash\n239\tcd /home/georg/powdr/results/pairing\n240\tPROVE_BIN=\"/home/georg/powdr/target/release/powdr_openvm_riscv\"\n241\t$PROVE_BIN prove --artifact apc000.cbor --input 0 --metrics after_apc000/metrics.json --recursion\n242\t$PROVE_BIN prove --artifact apc100.cbor --input 0 --metrics after_apc100/metrics.json --recursion\n243\t$PROVE_BIN prove --artifact apc300.cbor --input 0 --metrics after_apc300/metrics.json --recursion\n244\t```\n245\t\n246\tAnalyze with `spec.py`:\n247\t```bash\n248\tpython3 /home/georg/spec.py after_apc300/metrics.json after_apc300\n249\t```\n250\t\n251\t### Expected outcomes\n252\t- **Round 0 at APC 300**: 663ms -> 350-430ms (35-48% improvement)\n253\t- **Round 0 at APC 0**: 177ms -> 170-180ms (no regression; kernels already saturate GPU)\n254\t- **STARK excl trace at APC 300**: 2272ms -> 1950-2100ms (8-14% improvement)\n255\t- **STARK excl trace at APC 0**: ~2130ms (no regression)\n256\t- **Correctness**: prove+verify succeeds for all three APC configs\n257\t\n258\t### Profiling\n259\tRun nsight on APC 300 to verify concurrent kernel execution:\n260\t```bash\n261\tnsys profile --output after_apc300/nsys_report --force-overwrite true \\\n262\t    --trace cuda,nvtx,osrt --sample none --stats true \\\n263\t    -- $PROVE_BIN prove --artifact apc300.cbor --input 0 --recursion\n264\t```\n265\tCheck the timeline view: kernels from different streams should overlap temporally.\n266\t\n267\t## Rollback Criteria\n268\t\n269\t- **Less than 15% improvement** in Round 0 at APC 300 (i.e., Round 0 stays above 565ms): ROLLBACK. The multi-stream overhead would not be justified.\n270\t- **Any regression > 5%** in STARK excl trace at APC 0: ROLLBACK. The optimization must not hurt the non-APC case.\n271\t- **Correctness failure**: Any prove+verify failure: ROLLBACK immediately.\n272\t- **Memory OOM**: If the additional concurrent intermediate buffers cause GPU OOM, reduce `NUM_ROUND0_STREAMS` to 2 and re-test. If still OOM at 2 streams: ROLLBACK.\n273\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"toolu_01MQN4oFS5GMuCCr8dLJfzyH","session_id":"bf8cf1a6-3d58-4ca0-8a0c-442b3fb4c97c","uuid":"39af913a-dd4f-40c7-a1f5-6104abcf6a3b","timestamp":"2026-04-12T22:38:51.491Z"}
