{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01Ef3SiFDUr1kPaf9j8ugkvs","type":"tool_result","content":"130\t/// See [`crate::logup_zerocheck`] module docs for async-free/peak memory behavior.\n131\t#[allow(clippy::too_many_arguments)]\n132\tpub fn evaluate_round0_interactions_gpu<HS: GpuHashScheme>(\n133\t    pk: &DeviceStarkProvingKey<GenericGpuBackend<HS>>,\n134\t    symbolic: &SymbolicConstraints<F>,\n135\t    selectors_cube: &DeviceBuffer<F>,\n136\t    main_parts: &DeviceBuffer<*const F>,\n137\t    public_values: &DeviceBuffer<F>,\n138\t    eq_cube: *const EF,\n139\t    beta_pows: &[EF],\n140\t    eq_3bs: &[EF],\n141\t    skip_domain: u32,\n142\t    num_x: u32,\n143\t    height: u32,\n144\t    num_cosets: u32,\n145\t    g_shift: F,\n146\t    max_temp_bytes: usize,\n147\t) -> Result<DeviceBuffer<Frac<EF>>, Round0EvalError> {\n148\t    // Check if this trace has interactions\n149\t    if eq_3bs.is_empty() {\n150\t        return Ok(DeviceBuffer::new());\n151\t    }\n152\t    let large_domain = num_cosets * skip_domain;\n153\t\n154\t    // We create a new \"interactions DAG\" where the new .constraints are the interaction [count,\n155\t    // message_0, message_1, ..] expressions themselves, while the .interactions are empty\n156\t    // We track the indices with InteractionNode\n157\t\n158\t    // Copied from build_symbolic_constraints_dag to handle sorting of constraints\n159\t    // NOTE: For logup round0, the kernel uses weights indexed by rule_idx, not constraint_idx.\n160\t    // So we deduplicate constraint_idx and use dag_idx_to_rule_idx for weight mapping.\n161\t    let (rules, d_numer_weights, d_denom_weights, denom_sum_init) = {\n162\t        let mut dag_builder = SymbolicDagBuilder::new();\n163\t        let mut sorted_used_dag_idxs = Vec::new();\n164\t        for interaction in &symbolic.interactions {\n165\t            let count = dag_builder.add_expr(&interaction.count);\n166\t            sorted_used_dag_idxs.push(count);\n167\t            sorted_used_dag_idxs.extend(\n168\t                interaction\n169\t                    .message\n170\t                    .iter()\n171\t                    .map(|field_expr| dag_builder.add_expr(field_expr)),\n172\t            );\n173\t        }\n174\t        sorted_used_dag_idxs.sort();\n175\t        // Deduplicate for the dag since logup round0 kernel doesn't use used_nodes\n176\t        sorted_used_dag_idxs.dedup();\n177\t        let dag = SymbolicExpressionDag {\n178\t            nodes: dag_builder.nodes,\n179\t            constraint_idx: sorted_used_dag_idxs,\n180\t        };\n181\t        let rules = SymbolicRulesGpu::new(&dag, true);\n182\t        let mut numer_weights = vec![EF::ZERO; rules.rules.len()];\n183\t        let mut denom_weights = vec![EF::ZERO; rules.rules.len()];\n184\t        let mut denom_sum_init = EF::ZERO;\n185\t        for (interaction_idx, interaction) in symbolic.interactions.iter().enumerate() {\n186\t            // CAUTION: an expression node could be used in multiple interactions, and might even be\n187\t            // used as `count` in one, but message field in another. We only care about their\n188\t            // weighted sum with eq_3b, so we compute the weights ahead of time.\n189\t            let count_dag_idx =\n190\t                dag_builder.expr_to_idx[&(&interaction.count as *const SymbolicExpression<_>)];\n191\t            let count_rule_idx = rules.dag_idx_to_rule_idx[&count_dag_idx];\n192\t            numer_weights[count_rule_idx] += eq_3bs[interaction_idx];\n193\t            denom_sum_init += eq_3bs[interaction_idx]\n194\t                * beta_pows[interaction.message.len()]\n195\t                * F::from_u32(interaction.bus_index as u32 + 1);\n196\t\n197\t            for (message_idx, message) in interaction.message.iter().enumerate() {\n198\t                let message_dag_idx =\n199\t                    dag_builder.expr_to_idx[&(message as *const SymbolicExpression<_>)];\n200\t                let message_rule_idx = rules.dag_idx_to_rule_idx[&message_dag_idx];\n201\t                denom_weights[message_rule_idx] += eq_3bs[interaction_idx] * beta_pows[message_idx];\n202\t            }\n203\t        }\n204\t        let d_numer_weights = numer_weights.to_device()?;\n205\t        let d_denom_weights = denom_weights.to_device()?;\n206\t        (rules, d_numer_weights, d_denom_weights, denom_sum_init)\n207\t    };\n208\t\n209\t    let encoded_rules = rules.rules.iter().map(|c| c.encode()).collect_vec();"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"bf8cf1a6-3d58-4ca0-8a0c-442b3fb4c97c","uuid":"303ca8ee-e6da-4d5b-81c5-6405f6a2d45c","timestamp":"2026-04-12T22:41:48.758Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/home/georg/stark-backend/crates/cuda-backend/src/logup_zerocheck/round0.rs","content":"/// See [`crate::logup_zerocheck`] module docs for async-free/peak memory behavior.\n#[allow(clippy::too_many_arguments)]\npub fn evaluate_round0_interactions_gpu<HS: GpuHashScheme>(\n    pk: &DeviceStarkProvingKey<GenericGpuBackend<HS>>,\n    symbolic: &SymbolicConstraints<F>,\n    selectors_cube: &DeviceBuffer<F>,\n    main_parts: &DeviceBuffer<*const F>,\n    public_values: &DeviceBuffer<F>,\n    eq_cube: *const EF,\n    beta_pows: &[EF],\n    eq_3bs: &[EF],\n    skip_domain: u32,\n    num_x: u32,\n    height: u32,\n    num_cosets: u32,\n    g_shift: F,\n    max_temp_bytes: usize,\n) -> Result<DeviceBuffer<Frac<EF>>, Round0EvalError> {\n    // Check if this trace has interactions\n    if eq_3bs.is_empty() {\n        return Ok(DeviceBuffer::new());\n    }\n    let large_domain = num_cosets * skip_domain;\n\n    // We create a new \"interactions DAG\" where the new .constraints are the interaction [count,\n    // message_0, message_1, ..] expressions themselves, while the .interactions are empty\n    // We track the indices with InteractionNode\n\n    // Copied from build_symbolic_constraints_dag to handle sorting of constraints\n    // NOTE: For logup round0, the kernel uses weights indexed by rule_idx, not constraint_idx.\n    // So we deduplicate constraint_idx and use dag_idx_to_rule_idx for weight mapping.\n    let (rules, d_numer_weights, d_denom_weights, denom_sum_init) = {\n        let mut dag_builder = SymbolicDagBuilder::new();\n        let mut sorted_used_dag_idxs = Vec::new();\n        for interaction in &symbolic.interactions {\n            let count = dag_builder.add_expr(&interaction.count);\n            sorted_used_dag_idxs.push(count);\n            sorted_used_dag_idxs.extend(\n                interaction\n                    .message\n                    .iter()\n                    .map(|field_expr| dag_builder.add_expr(field_expr)),\n            );\n        }\n        sorted_used_dag_idxs.sort();\n        // Deduplicate for the dag since logup round0 kernel doesn't use used_nodes\n        sorted_used_dag_idxs.dedup();\n        let dag = SymbolicExpressionDag {\n            nodes: dag_builder.nodes,\n            constraint_idx: sorted_used_dag_idxs,\n        };\n        let rules = SymbolicRulesGpu::new(&dag, true);\n        let mut numer_weights = vec![EF::ZERO; rules.rules.len()];\n        let mut denom_weights = vec![EF::ZERO; rules.rules.len()];\n        let mut denom_sum_init = EF::ZERO;\n        for (interaction_idx, interaction) in symbolic.interactions.iter().enumerate() {\n            // CAUTION: an expression node could be used in multiple interactions, and might even be\n            // used as `count` in one, but message field in another. We only care about their\n            // weighted sum with eq_3b, so we compute the weights ahead of time.\n            let count_dag_idx =\n                dag_builder.expr_to_idx[&(&interaction.count as *const SymbolicExpression<_>)];\n            let count_rule_idx = rules.dag_idx_to_rule_idx[&count_dag_idx];\n            numer_weights[count_rule_idx] += eq_3bs[interaction_idx];\n            denom_sum_init += eq_3bs[interaction_idx]\n                * beta_pows[interaction.message.len()]\n                * F::from_u32(interaction.bus_index as u32 + 1);\n\n            for (message_idx, message) in interaction.message.iter().enumerate() {\n                let message_dag_idx =\n                    dag_builder.expr_to_idx[&(message as *const SymbolicExpression<_>)];\n                let message_rule_idx = rules.dag_idx_to_rule_idx[&message_dag_idx];\n                denom_weights[message_rule_idx] += eq_3bs[interaction_idx] * beta_pows[message_idx];\n            }\n        }\n        let d_numer_weights = numer_weights.to_device()?;\n        let d_denom_weights = denom_weights.to_device()?;\n        (rules, d_numer_weights, d_denom_weights, denom_sum_init)\n    };\n\n    let encoded_rules = rules.rules.iter().map(|c| c.encode()).collect_vec();","numLines":80,"startLine":130,"totalLines":276}}}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-6","id":"msg_01HNMSvGaWRocdSmJ9StWwAT","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Now I can see the full picture. Let me update the plan with all the review fixes:\n\n1. `beta_pows` is `&[EF]` (line 139, and `self.beta_pows` is `Vec<EF>` at line 409)\n2. `n_per_trace` is `Vec<isize>` (line 423)\n3. The interaction rule building (lines 161-207) does significant CPU work including:\n   - SymbolicDagBuilder + dag construction\n   - SymbolicRulesGpu::new()\n   - Weight computation\n   - 2 H2D copies (d_numer_weights, d_denom_weights)\n4. The interaction function also does more GPU allocations (lines 204-205, 209-251)\n\nThe memory manager mutex is a real bottleneck—each AIR triggers roughly 10 malloc and 10 free calls, so with 4 threads running concurrently that's potentially 40 lock acquisitions competing. Pre-allocating per-thread buffers for intermediates and temp_sums could help, but the challenge is that buffer sizes vary per AIR depending on parameters like `buffer_size`, `skip_domain`, `num_x`, and `num_cosets`, so I'd need to compute those sizes upfront.\n\nLooking at the constraint and interaction evaluation functions, I can see where the buffers come from—`intermediates` and `temp_sums_buffer` are sized based on helper functions, and `sp_evals` depends on `num_cosets * skip_domain`. Pre-allocating would require a preliminary pass to find the maximum sizes across all AIRs in each thread's chunk, which adds complexity. For now, I'll treat the mutex contention as a known limitation and mark buffer pre-allocation as a follow-on optimization rather than part of the initial implementation.\n\nThe main fix is correcting the `max_temp_bytes` division, then I can adjust the performance estimates accordingly.","signature":""}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2534,"cache_read_input_tokens":153929,"cac