{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01Ak1jwhodML76ukK8YCRrgS","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t# 2026-04-13-0100-multistream-round0-parallel\n2\t\n3\tRound 0 constraint evaluation processes 623 AIRs sequentially on a single CUDA stream (cudaStreamPerThread). At APC 300, most AIRs are tiny (height 8-64), so each kernel uses 1-4 of the RTX 4090's 128 SMs — GPU throughput drops 10.7x per cell vs APC 0. By processing AIRs across N OS threads (each with its own per-thread CUDA stream), small kernels from different streams execute concurrently on idle SMs, recovering GPU utilization and overlapping CPU metadata preparation with GPU execution. This is expected to reduce Round 0 from ~663ms to ~350-430ms (35-48% improvement), yielding an 8-14% reduction in STARK excl trace.\n4\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"bf8cf1a6-3d58-4ca0-8a0c-442b3fb4c97c","uuid":"b97e9204-da40-41a4-9e9c-d96b0e69e4ee","timestamp":"2026-04-12T22:47:42.505Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/home/georg/stark-backend/autoopt-results/task.md","content":"# 2026-04-13-0100-multistream-round0-parallel\n\nRound 0 constraint evaluation processes 623 AIRs sequentially on a single CUDA stream (cudaStreamPerThread). At APC 300, most AIRs are tiny (height 8-64), so each kernel uses 1-4 of the RTX 4090's 128 SMs — GPU throughput drops 10.7x per cell vs APC 0. By processing AIRs across N OS threads (each with its own per-thread CUDA stream), small kernels from different streams execute concurrently on idle SMs, recovering GPU utilization and overlapping CPU metadata preparation with GPU execution. This is expected to reduce Round 0 from ~663ms to ~350-430ms (35-48% improvement), yielding an 8-14% reduction in STARK excl trace.\n","numLines":4,"startLine":1,"totalLines":4}}}
